 \paragraph{Oracle reference.}
 \revred{The historical oracle-risk Top-3-from-10 reference uses ground-truth metrics to select among ten full-SCC attempts. For each three-attempt subset of valid outputs, it computes mean Root@3, Risk-any, and Risk-all. Selection lexicographically maximizes the minimum of these three metrics, their mean, and mean compression. With fewer than three valid attempts, it uses all valid attempts; with none, binary metrics are zero. Reported metrics average the selected attempts without pooling their nodes or subgraphs. This oracle selection requires ground truth, unlike deployable One-shot and LEA, and incurs the computation of ten attempts.}
 
